# Template for secrets/turing-api.env — the runtime env for the Turing API (the
# FastAPI service in turing-api/). Real file is gitignored.
#
# This is the ONE template for that service. Every environment variable the API
# reads is listed below, uncommented when it must be set and commented out when
# the default is what the cluster runs; scripts/check-turing-env.mjs fails CI if
# turing-api/ reads a name that is missing here (or reads one name at two sites).
#
# Unlike next.env / convex.env, this file is not pushed by `pnpm secrets:sync`
# because the Turing cluster is not a managed platform we can talk to over an
# API. Edit values here, then scp the file to the cluster:
#
#   scp secrets/turing-api.env <user>@<turing-host>:~/tom.quest/turing-api/.env


# --- service ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shared API key. Must match TURING_API_KEY in next.env and convex.env. The API
# refuses to start without it.
TURING_API_KEY=

# Port the API binds on 127.0.0.1 (the co-located cloudflared tunnel reaches it).
# API_PORT=8000

# Root that GET /file and GET /dirs are confined to. Defaults to $HOME; paths that
# escape it, and secret-bearing names (.env/.pem/.key, .ssh/.aws/.gnupg), are
# refused inside it either way.
# TURING_FILE_ROOT=$HOME


# --- the ComplexMultiTrigger (CMT) roots --------------------------------------

# The CMT checkout (boolean_backdoor package root) that BOTH cluster-facing
# surfaces run jobs from: the boolback snapshot build and the Forge train/serve
# jobs cd here. One name for one checkout — set it and both surfaces move
# together. (Until 2026-08-29 the Forge side read this name and the boolback side
# read BOOLBACK_BUILDER_REPO_DIR, so setting one left the other on its default.)
BOOLEAN_BACKDOOR_REPO=$HOME/booleanbackdoors/ComplexMultiTrigger

# The CMT artifact tree. Every path the API serves is pinned under it, and Forge
# run dirs live in $BOOLEAN_BACKDOOR_OUTPUT/forge/<run_id>/. No default: the API
# raises rather than serve some other tree's data.
BOOLEAN_BACKDOOR_OUTPUT=$HOME/booleanbackdoors/cmt-output


# --- boolback snapshot surface ------------------------------------------------

# Conda env the CMT builder (and, by default, the Forge jobs) run in.
# BOOLBACK_BUILDER_CONDA_ENV=boolback

# Where built .gz snapshots and per-dir submit markers are written. The sbatch
# wrapper also writes its build-%j.out logs here.
# BOOLBACK_CACHE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/boolback-snapshots

# The sbatch wrapper that runs the snapshot builder on a CPU compute node.
# Defaults to the one shipped beside the module, turing-api/boolback_build.sbatch.
# BOOLBACK_BUILD_SBATCH=/abs/path/boolback_build.sbatch


# --- Forge surface (Track B) --------------------------------------------------

# Override the bundled sbatch wrappers (default: turing-api/forge_scripts/*.sbatch).
# FORGE_TRAIN_SBATCH=/abs/path/forge_train.sbatch
# FORGE_SERVE_SBATCH=/abs/path/forge_serve.sbatch

# Read by forge_serve.sbatch on the compute node: the conda env the vLLM server
# runs in. Falls back to BOOLBACK_BUILDER_CONDA_ENV.
# FORGE_SERVE_CONDA_ENV=boolback

# vLLM serve job: the port bound on the compute node (reachable from the login
# node over the cluster LAN) and the idle-release window in seconds (the wrapper
# scancels itself after this long with no /forge/chat heartbeat touch).
# FORGE_SERVE_PORT=8765
# FORGE_SERVE_IDLE_SECS=600

# Login-node -> compute-node probe/chat timeouts (seconds).
# FORGE_PROBE_TIMEOUT=4
# FORGE_CHAT_TIMEOUT=120

# squeue %N returns a bare Slurm nodename ("gpu-5-43") that does not resolve from
# the login node, so this domain is appended to bare names to reach the serving
# node. Set it empty to disable, on a cluster whose squeue returns routable names.
# FORGE_NODE_DOMAIN=.int.turing.wpi.edu
